{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>בְּרָב־דְבָרִים</b> — when one speaks much, he produces [material] for the hater of slander to escape." "<b>לֹא יֶחְדַּל־פָּשַׁע</b> — much, meaning he cannot take back what he has spoken and make it cease, and it saves him [from consequences] before him." "<b>וְחֹשֵׂךְ שְׂפָתָיו</b> — from words of slander — <b>מַשְׂכִּיל</b>, in contrast to <b>כְּסִיל</b>."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Reading להנצל לשנוא מן הדבה as 'to escape the slanderer'; the syntax is compressed and the parsing uncertain.", 1 "The clause ותנצלהו לפניו is obscure; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:57.532224219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}